{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread","id":40564,"title":"Demon The Fallen: The Questions Thread!!!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-01T10:15:51-08:00","id":40564,"title":"Demon The Fallen: The Questions Thread!!!","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sYxbSRpVJ3s\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sYxbSRpVJ3s\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sYxbSRpVJ3s\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sYxbSRpVJ3s </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Welcome to the DtF Question thread, im Yer host and now lets ask some questions.<br /> <br /> 1._ Demons are famous for being stuck in The Abysm, a place so horrible that torn them inside out and drive them utterly Insane, right?, Does this means that powers like dementation work on a demon?<br /> 2._ Can a supernatural being enter The Abysm? and what would be the side effects if he does so?<br /> 3._ If a human has Faith Potential and he belives that the cereal is a god, could he exorcise a demon with cereal? (dont ask why)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T10:48:30-08:00","id":40579,"title":"","content":"1) I haven't touched DtF since around 2005 so I can't remember. I think it's possible but depends on the strength of the user and victim.<br /> <br /> 2) Given where the Abyss is located, it would be <i>incredibly </i>difficult and dangerous to reach. And given that along with the nature of that place it begs the question why would <i>anyone</i> want to go the Abyss? That said given what it did to the Fallen, the best outcome would be the supernatural being would come out insane.<br /> <br /> 3) ...No, not unless that person has the True Faith merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T15:48:51-08:00","id":40771,"title":"","content":"1) Nope. The Fallen are immune to all mental manipulation. This includes Dementation, Presence, Domination etc.<br /> <br /> 2) Can you get in ? Yes. Do you want to ? No. Remember: The Fallen are the weakest and MOST sane of the inhabitants of that place. Seriously, you don't want to go there.<br /> <br /> 3) With the True Faith merit (and a ST who likes that sort of humor in his game), yes. If not, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T20:48:13-08:00","id":40904,"title":"","content":"can a werewolf exorcise a demon through a gift (i belive theres a gift that pulls an spirit out of something)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T21:36:02-08:00","id":40915,"title":"","content":"I'd say no as the Fallen are not the same as Umbral spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T06:59:27-08:00","id":41083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread?p=40904#post40904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can a werewolf exorcise a demon through a gift (i belive theres a gift that pulls an spirit out of something)</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say yes, because an Earthbound in the Book of the same name was keeping a low profile from a group of Black Spirals because he new they could bind him with their spirit magics. As in the case of Fomori it probably kills the recipient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T07:08:28-08:00","id":41087,"title":"","content":"1. I really want to say no, but I will have to stick with probably not. Demons, as long as they have a faith point are immune to becoming puppets, but high Torment powers give them points of Torment. Then again that torment is fueled by the hate and insanity they learned from the Abyss itself, so it's anyone's guess if Dementation could break through the cracks in their armor, even just a little bit. 2. Instant transformation into Nephandi, or what have you. And that's only if they come back. 3. Depends on the back story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:40:08-08:00","id":41418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread?p=41083#post41083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I would say yes, because an Earthbound in the Book of the same name was keeping a low profile from a group of Black Spirals because he new they could bind him with their spirit magics. As in the case of Fomori it probably kills the recipient.</div> </div> </div> </div>With fomori, it &quot;merely&quot; has a high likelihood of killing the receipient. One health level of unsoakable aggravated is inflicted each turn for ten turns. You can try to heal some part of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T05:54:46-08:00","id":41661,"title":"","content":"1 dementaion would not work but i think presence might. im not sure<br /> 2 lasombra (at least methusellahs) can enter the abyss(althought not stated its heavily implies that its the same abyss.) as for other splats i not sure, thought presumably a mage would be able to enter if he knew what he was doing.<br /> 3 wel businessman who belive in the power of money can affect vampires with a credit card. so i guess it may be possible<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T05:56:16-08:00","id":41662,"title":"","content":"also about exorcising a demon , i think it would be possible. after all even baali can do it, so why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:53:58-08:00","id":41712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread?p=41661#post41661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 wel businessman who belive in the power of money can affect vampires with a credit card. so i guess it may be possible</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's an example of the True Faith merit, not their Faith rating. And like I said if someone has the merit than yes they can do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T08:26:22-08:00","id":41728,"title":"","content":"oh yeah youre right, always confused those 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T11:37:48-07:00","id":102067,"title":"","content":"Each of the Seven Houses has a particular weaknesses, cursorily described (I'm considering the core book). Where is the crunch? I mean, where are the mechanical aspect of those weaknesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T17:15:42-07:00","id":102261,"title":"","content":"1. Seeing how Mage's are still considered to be human is it possible for a Fallen to possess the body of a Mage and gain access to their powers?<br /> <br /> 2. If a Fallen becomes an Earthbound does he automatically become truly evil and malevolent or does he have time to find a new human vessel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2256,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","user":"Goblin404","date":". 03-30-2014, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2256-goblin404","name":"Goblin404","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2256_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-30T18:04:39-07:00","id":102284,"title":"","content":"1. No. When a Fallen possesses a body, they either expel or repress the soul already there. Any powers a Mage may have had disappear with their soul. That said, such a host is capable of having much more powerful Fallen than your average joe, due to their Faith Potential, which is higher than any other humans. For this reason, mages are sought out as hosts or thralls by powerful Fallen.<br /> <br /> 2. No, Fallen don't immediately go bad if they somehow become Earthbound. But without the mediating influence of human feelings/memories, it is hard not to be overwhelmed by Torment. Generally though, they don't become Earthbound at all. If the host body of a Fallen dies, they can seek out the nearest avaliable host and possess that. Only if the Fallen somehow become too powerful to inhabit human bodies, will they have to bind themselves to something else and thus become Earthbound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T09:34:58-07:00","id":102707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primal Flame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread?p=102067#post102067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each of the Seven Houses has a particular weaknesses, cursorily described (I'm considering the core book). Where is the crunch? I mean, where are the mechanical aspect of those weaknesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaknesses are really more a matter of roleplay for DtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/78-bloodarmor","name":"BloodArmor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar78_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T18:10:16-07:00","id":124172,"title":"","content":"On the old forums, there was a thread that toyed around with making new Evocations. Is anyone still working on that, or would anyone be interested in critiquing some of my efforts in that regard?<br /> <br /> <b>Awakening 1/2: Life At a Glance</b><br /> Once guardians of life, the Scourges can diagnose a subject's frailties with a look.<br /> SYSTEM: Roll Perception + Medicine. Success reveals what general sort of injuries, diseases, and other health concerns the patient has, as well as their current Health Levels. Each extra success pinpoints the exact nature of a problem, such as identifying a poison, spotting a malignant tumor, or sensing a minor bone fracture.<br /> TORMENT: Scourges who have embraced death and disease instead use this power to pinpoint a target's weak spots. Every two successes adds one level of damage to the demon's next effort to harm the target, as they assault the revealed weaknesses.<br /> <br /> <b>Light 2: Ranging Eye</b><br /> With precise manipulation of light, Fiends can see around corners, under doors, behind themselves, and from high overhead.<br /> SYSTEM: Roll Perception + Science. The Fiend may designate a point within line-of-sight, no further away than 10 yards per success, from which they can view in all directions, replacing their normal vision. This lasts as long as the Fiend's body stays in one place, and they maintain focus.<br /> TORMENT: A monstrous Fiend twists light violently, creating a visible distortion that draws the attention of even normal humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:02:31-07:00","id":142693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/40564-demon-the-fallen-the-questions-thread?p=102284#post102284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. No. When a Fallen possesses a body, they either expel or repress the soul already there. Any powers a Mage may have had disappear with their soul. That said, such a host is capable of having much more powerful Fallen than your average joe, due to their Faith Potential, which is higher than any other humans. For this reason, mages are sought out as hosts or thralls by powerful Fallen.<br /> <br /> 2. No, Fallen don't immediately go bad if they somehow become Earthbound. But without the mediating influence of human feelings/memories, it is hard not to be overwhelmed by Torment. Generally though, they don't become Earthbound at all. If the host body of a Fallen dies, they can seek out the nearest avaliable host and possess that. Only if the Fallen somehow become too powerful to inhabit human bodies, will they have to bind themselves to something else and thus become Earthbound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earthbound generally refers to the big bads of Demon. Whereas earthbound (E vs e) refers to any of the fallen stuck in a reliquary instead of a host. Also, like point #2 states, even if the fallen who just possessed a reliquary was a good guy before, he's about to be Torment 10 real fast, and once you get there, you cant inhabit mortals anymore.<br /> Demon: Earthbound supplement sets forth rules that might actually let you play an earthbound, but I've never even seen a game of Demon played, much less with Earthbound :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/771-starmage21","name":"Starmage21","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar771_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}